<title>TURKEY: TURKISH 287-D T-BILL YIELD EASES TO 96.47 PCT.</title>
<headline>TURKISH 287-D T-BILL YIELD EASES TO 96.47 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield in the Turkish treasury's 287-day bill auction fell to 96.47 percent on Tuesday from 99.24 percent in the previous 399-day bond auction on January 21.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : November 19, 1997</p>
<p>	Amount			: 196.4 trln lira</p>
<p>	Coupon			: -</p>
<p>	Minimum yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Maximum yield	     : 96.47</p>
<p>	Average yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Bid amount/cover	  : 229.3 trln</p>
<p>	Lowest accepted price   : 58,715 lira</p>
<p>Pct allocated at lowest price : -</p>
<p>	Payment date		: February 5, 1997</p>
<p>--Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75 EKS</p>
